    "chunk_size_bytes": 1366,
    "chunk_text": "Robust progress in China-Sri Lanka relations: Ambassador Qi\n\nOn the occasion of the upcoming Year of the Horse, I am delighted to gather with you all to ring out the old and usher in the new. On behalf of the Chinese Embassy in Sri Lanka, I would like to extend festive greetings to all the overseas Chinese, staff of Chinese companies and Chinese students in Sri Lanka. I also wish to express sincere appreciation to friends from all walks of life who have consistently cared for and supported the growth of China-Sri Lanka relations.\n\nAmong all festivals, the Spring Festival holds the highest place. Among all seasons, spring stands as the first. As the most ancient, grand and important traditional festival in China, the Spring Festival represents the cultural roots and emotional bonds of the Chinese people, embodies their devotion to family and country, and conveys the values of peace, goodwill and harmony. Although originating in China, the Spring Festival now belongs to the world. Having been inscribed on UNESCO\u2019s Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, its global influence continues to grow. The Spring Festival is increasingly becoming a window to showcase Chinese culture and a bridge for cultural exchange and mutual learning among civilisations.\n\nExtraordinary chapter on the journey toward building a great country"
