    "chunk_text": "The Purification Sector saw Haycarb PLC secure the Overall Winner Award for the \u2018Innovation of Specialty Activated Carbon for Silicon-Carbon Composites used as Next Generation Anode Materials in Lithium-Ion Batteries\u2019, through the introduction of the HCE 400 Series to improve energy density and battery life. The initiative also secured the Innovation Category Award, marking a strategic step into advanced materials aligned with the growth trajectory of global battery and energy storage markets.\n\nFrom the Textiles Sector, Hayleys Fabric PLC was recognised for developing a Smart Energy Saving System for Stenter Machines \u2013 an automated, low-investment solution that cuts idle-time energy loss in one of the plant\u2019s most power-intensive processes. The initiative delivers material reductions in thermal and electrical consumption, lowers reliance on imported fuels and avoids 159,600 kg CO\u2082e emissions per machine annually, aligning with Net Zero 2050 and SBTi pathways. The project secured the ESG Category Award.\n\nFrom the Transportation and Logistics Sector, K&A Logistics \u2013 a joint venture between Hayleys Advantis Group and Karnaphuli Group \u2013 received the Service Excellence Award for \u2018Establishing 3PL Market Leadership through Record Growth and Strategic Diversification in Bangladesh\u2019. The project was recognised for its contribution to service reliability and for positioning Advantis as a capable regional logistics partner within the South Asian supply chain ecosystem.\n\nThe Hayleys Chairman\u2019s Awards 2025 celebrated bold innovation, operational excellence and meaningful social impact across sectors, highlighting projects that redefine competitiveness, reinforce sustainability and position Sri Lanka as a leader in global manufacturing and services."
