    "chunk_size_bytes": 919,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Japan to formalise economic policy dialogue with MoU\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers at their meeting on Monday approved signing a memorandum of understanding (MoU) with Japan on economic policy dialogue.\n\n\u201cThe agreement is to be signed on 16 February with the objective of promoting comprehensive relations between Sri Lanka and Japan, and as part of the efforts to promote and strengthen trade, investments and economic development,\u201d Cabinet Spokesman and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa said at the weekly post-Cabinet meeting media briefing yesterday.\n\nHe said discussions between the two countries have been ongoing to position Sri Lanka as a strategic export-oriented economic corridor, integrating it into the South Asian markets.\n\nThe proposal to this effect submitted by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe was approved by the Cabinet of Ministers."
